This rule defines the project conventions for the Techniques of Artificial Intelligence (TIA) course.

## Project Structure

This is an educational course project containing:

- **PDFs**: Course materials, lecture slides, programs
- **Jupyter Notebooks**: Code examples and exercises
- **Modules**:
  - NLP Intro (Natural Language Processing)
  - Machine Learning
  - Neural Networks
  - Image Digital Processing
  - Expert Systems

## File Organization

- Course materials organized by module in separate directories
- PDFs: `*.pdf` files for theory and slides
- Notebooks: `*.ipynb` files for practical exercises
- Data: Supporting datasets in appropriate folders

## Working with Jupyter Notebooks

- Use standard Jupyter notebook structure
- Include clear markdown headers for explanations
- Comment code thoroughly for learning purposes
- Keep cells focused and modular

## Conventions

- Keep original file naming from course
- Follow course naming conventions for new files
- Use Spanish for comments and documentation when appropriate